# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fork additions. Everything above this line is upstream's own ignore list at
# tag v3.1.1, all ten patterns in their original order, kept verbatim. None was
# removed, reordered relative to another, or weakened.
#
# The rules below are this fork's own build outputs. This package compiles with
# Zig and never runs CMake, so upstream's rules are kept because upstream's tree
# depends on them, not because this build produces them.
#
# None of the paths below is named in build.zig.zon `.paths`, so an ignored path
# can never become part of the package a dependent fetches.
#
# Directories rather than single files, because a normal `zig build` creates
# directories and a normal `zig build` must not dirty the tree.
.zig-cache/
zig-out/
# Zig 0.16 materialises a fetched dependency tree beside the package root.
# This package declares no dependencies, so this exists only so that a future
# one cannot commit a fetched tree.
zig-pkg/

# The consumer package builds inside this repository and has its own cache and
# output tree. It is ignored here as well as in consumer/.gitignore, so a build
# run from the repository root cannot commit it by accident.
consumer/.zig-cache/
consumer/zig-out/
consumer/zig-pkg/

# Nix and devenv working-tree artefacts. `nix build` writes `result` (and
# `result-1`, `result-2`, ... on a rebuild) into the directory that asked for
# it, and `devenv` writes its resolved inputs and its state beside the project.
# `devenv.lock` and `flake.lock` are deliberately *not* here: they are real
# inputs, they belong to the driver, and ignoring them would be the wrong way
# to keep a build out of a commit.
result
result-*
.devenv/
.devenv.flake.nix
.devenv.flakes/
devenv.local.nix
